  "id": "inferential-validity",
  "term": "inferential validity",
  "definition": "Inferential validity is the extent to which conclusions drawn from data analysis are trustworthy, including whether estimates and statistical uncertainty accurately reflect the underlying data. It can be weakened when problems such as missing data distort results and lead to biased findings.",
